## Why GPL-2.0 and not a choice

The core is a port of the Linux kernel's `fs/ntfs` driver (ntfsplus, Linux 7.1,
by Namjae Jeon and contributors), vendored unmodified under `upstream/` and
ported under `core/ntfs/` and `core/vfs/`. That code is GPL-2.0, so this work is
a derivative of it and carries the same licence. It is not a licence we picked;
it is the one we inherited, and it is why this driver can exist at all — no
other complete, GPL-licensed NTFS write implementation does.

